s), the intangible nature of Bitcoin becomes less of a barrier and more of a feature. Finally, volatility tends to decrease as market capitalization grows and liquidity deepens. Bitcoin is still relatively young and small compared to global fiat markets. As adoption increases, price swings are likely to moderate. Ten years ago, a 20% daily move was common; now, a 5% move is notable. So while Bitcoin today isn't ready to replace your local currency for buying groceries tomorrow, it is evolving rapidly. For savings and long-term wealth preservation, its track record over the past decade is actually quite strong. And for everyday use, the infrastructure to manage volatility is already being built.
