 even if they don't make headlines. 4. **The most honest thing I can say is this:** You might be right that most people won't see Bitcoin as anything more than a speculative gamble for years, maybe even decades. But that doesn't mean it isn't a sustainable and viable alternative to fiat. It means it's still early. The question isn't whether the majority believes today—it's whether the system is robust enough to survive and grow until the majority has a reason to look more closely. I'm not asking you to bet your savings on that. But I am asking you to consider that what looks like a gamble from the outside can be a carefully designed, resilient system from the inside. And systems like that have a way of outlasting the skepticism that surrounds them.
