dit card. **Finally, I want to acknowledge that your skepticism is not just reasonable—it's wise.** If I had watched three friends lose their down payments, I'd be skeptical too. I wouldn't expect you to trust Bitcoin just because I explained its properties. Trust has to be earned, and for you, Bitcoin hasn't earned it yet. All I can say is this: Bitcoin's long-term viability doesn't depend on everyone using it perfectly. It depends on the system itself being sound. And that system has survived far worse crashes than the one your friends experienced. But that doesn't make their loss any less real, and I'm sorry they went through it.
